      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that, but i'm also seeing some older medical literature and prep materials that mention physiological differences in how certain ethnicities react to treatments or even their baseline pain thresholds. even if it's considered outdated now, it's still showing up in these old texts. as a study aid, can you explain the logic behind those older theories? like, what were the actual medical justifications they used for claiming certain groups had different pain tolerances or different vascular responses? i just want to understand the history of these clinical observations so i don't confuse them with modern standards.",
